From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 12:29:33 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] drm/edid: list frame-sequential modes from stereo detailed
 timings

A detailed timing whose stereo flags say field sequential (E-EDID 1.4,
section 3.10.2, Table 3.22: bits 6:5 = 01b with the right image, or 10b
with the left image, while the stereo sync signal is 1, bit 0 clear) is a
timing the sink shows in stereo, one eye per frame. That is the
frame-sequential layout DRM can now describe, so add a copy of such a
timing's mode with DRM_MODE_FLAG_3D_FRAME_SEQUENTIAL, next to its 2D
mode, never preferred.

The sync polarity belongs to the sideband stereo sync signal; on
DisplayPort the source names the eye of each frame in-band (MSA MISC1),
so both values give the same mode. Interlaced timings are left out: the
table speaks of fields, and a field of an interlaced timing is half a
frame. The 2-way, 4-way and side by side interleaved values have no DRM
layout yet and add no stereo mode.

The mode is listed only on connectors whose driver accepts frame
sequential stereo; there are none yet.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/drm_edid.c | 37 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 37 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_edid.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_edid.c
index 74b069391..c791a38e2 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_edid.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_edid.c
@@ -4126,6 +4126,40 @@ add_cvt_modes(struct drm_connector *connector, const struct drm_edid *drm_edid)
 static void fixup_detailed_cea_mode_clock(struct drm_connector *connector,
 					  struct drm_display_mode *mode);
 
+/*
+ * A detailed timing whose stereo flags say field sequential, with either
+ * polarity of the stereo sync signal (E-EDID 1.4, Table 3.22), is also a
+ * frame-sequential mode: the sink takes the eyes in turn, one per frame of the
+ * timing. Interlaced timings are left out, as a field there is half a frame.
+ * The interleaved values have no DRM layout yet.
+ */
+static int
+add_detailed_stereo_mode(struct drm_connector *connector,
+			 const struct detailed_timing *timing,
+			 const struct drm_display_mode *mode)
+{
+	const struct detailed_pixel_timing *pt = &timing->data.pixel_data;
+	u8 stereo = pt->misc & DRM_EDID_PT_STEREO_MASK;
+	struct drm_display_mode *newmode;
+
+	if (stereo != DRM_EDID_PT_STEREO_FIELD_SEQ_RIGHT &&
+	    stereo != DRM_EDID_PT_STEREO_FIELD_SEQ_LEFT)
+		return 0;
+
+	if (mode->flags & DRM_MODE_FLAG_INTERLACE)
+		return 0;
+
+	newmode = drm_mode_duplicate(connector->dev, mode);
+	if (!newmode)
+		return 0;
+
+	newmode->type &= ~DRM_MODE_TYPE_PREFERRED;
+	newmode->flags |= DRM_MODE_FLAG_3D_FRAME_SEQUENTIAL;
+	drm_mode_probed_add(connector, newmode);
+
+	return 1;
+}
+
 static void
 do_detailed_mode(const struct detailed_timing *timing, void *c)
 {
@@ -4153,6 +4187,9 @@ do_detailed_mode(const struct detailed_timing *timing, void *c)
 	drm_mode_probed_add(closure->connector, newmode);
 	closure->modes++;
 	closure->preferred = false;
+
+	closure->modes += add_detailed_stereo_mode(closure->connector, timing,
+						   newmode);
 }
 
